cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "telemetryool: operational out-of-limit checking and a matched-false-alarm-rate detector comparison harness"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Out-of-limit checking for housekeeping telemetry with the full operational
  semantics (soft and hard limits, per-channel validity masks, persistence and
  debounce counts, mode-dependent limit tables), EWMA and CUSUM drift detection
  with thresholds designed to a stated false-alarm rate rather than tuned,
  offline change-point detection with a Monte-Carlo-calibrated threshold, and a
  harness that brings every detector to the same window false-alarm probability
  on independent nominal data before comparing detection delay. Multivariate
  novelty detection is included and benchmarked against the classical baselines
  at the matched operating point, with full confusion matrices and
  window-level ROC. Validation level 2, research grade. Not flight-qualified,
  not certified, not approved for operational aerospace use.
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
  - telemetry
  - out-of-limit
  - limit-checking
  - false-alarm-rate
  - cusum
  - ewma
  - change-point
  - novelty-detection
  - statistical-process-control
